.TH ZERODDS-WS-BRIDGED.YAML 5 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-ws-bridged.yaml \- configuration file for zerodds-ws-bridged(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/zerodds/ws-bridged.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
YAML document describing how the WebSocket bridge daemon binds DDS topics to
WebSocket URLs. The schema is the one of
.IR zerodds-ws-bridge-1.0 " \(sc3;"
the parser that reads it is
.IR crates/websocket-bridge/src/daemon/config.rs::load_from_str .
.PP
Top-level keys:
.BR listen ", " domain ", " log_level ", " tls ", " auth ", " metrics ", " topics .
.PP
An unknown top-level key is
.I not
a parse error. The daemon logs a WARN line on stderr and starts with the
defaults for everything the unknown key was meant to configure. A typo in a
key therefore does not abort the start \(em watch the WARN log.
.PP
.BI ${VAR} " and " ${VAR:-default}
are substituted from the environment before the document is parsed.
.SH KEYS
.SS Top level
.TP
.B listen
WebSocket listen address, e.g.
.IR "0.0.0.0:8080" .
.TP
.B domain
Integer DDS domain ID. Default
.IR 0 .
.TP
.B log_level
.IR trace " | " debug " | " info " | " warn " | " error .
A
.B \-\-log\-level
on the command line wins over this key.
.SS tls
.TP
.B enabled
Boolean. When true,
.BR cert_file " and " key_file
must point to PEM material readable by user
.IR zerodds .
.TP
.B cert_file
Server certificate chain, PEM.
.TP
.B key_file
Server private key, PEM.
.TP
.B client_ca_file
Trust anchor for client certificates. Setting it turns on mTLS.
.SS auth
.TP
.B mode
.IR none " | " bearer " | " jwt " | " mtls " (\(sc7.2)."
For
.IR mtls ,
.B tls.enabled
and
.B tls.client_ca_file
are required; the subject is the client certificate's subject DN (RFC 4514);
an ACL entry may name its fingerprint
.I mtls:<SHA-256 hex>
instead.
.TP
.B bearer_token
Shared token accepted in the
.I Authorization
header when
.B mode
is
.IR bearer .
.TP
.B bearer_subject
Subject every connection authenticated by that single token runs as.
.TP
.B jwt
Sub-map for
.BR jwt :
.B public_key
(PEM file, PKCS#1 or SubjectPublicKeyInfo, RS256),
.BR issuer ,
.BR audience ,
.B required_claim
.RI ( claim=value ;
a space-separated claim such as
.I scope
matches when it contains the value).
.I exp
and
.I nbf
are enforced with 60 s leeway. The subject is the
.I sub
claim. Without
.B public_key
the daemon does not start (exit 1).
.I bearer
is single-subject; for per-user identities use
.IR jwt .
.SS metrics
.TP
.B enabled
Boolean. Turns on the admin endpoint serving
.IR /metrics ", " /catalog " and " /healthz .
.TP
.B listen
Admin listen address. Default
.IR "127.0.0.1:9091"
when
.B enabled
is true; each bridge daemon has its own port, so several run on one
host without a collision.
The key is
.BR listen ,
not
.IR address .
.SS topics (list)
Each entry maps one DDS topic to one WebSocket path.
.TP
.B name
DDS topic name.
.TP
.B type
Fully-qualified IDL type. Defaults to
.BR name .
.TP
.B direction
.IR in " | " out " | " bidir .
.I in
carries frames from WebSocket clients into DDS (the daemon creates a
DataWriter),
.I out
carries DDS samples to subscribed clients (a DataReader),
.I bidir
both. Default
.IR bidir .
A publish to a topic that is not bridged into DDS, or a subscribe to one
that is not bridged out of DDS, is answered with an error frame
(code 404, reason
.I not-bridged-into-dds
or
.IR not-bridged-out-of-dds ).
.TP
.B ws_path
HTTP path clients connect to. Defaults to
.IR /topics/<slug-of-name> .
.TP
.B qos
Sub-map with
.B reliability
.RI ( reliable " | " best_effort ),
.B durability
.RI ( volatile " | " transient_local )
and
.B history
carrying
.BR depth .
.TP
.B acl
Per-topic access control, sub-map with the subject lists
.BR read " and " write .
.B acl
belongs to the topic entry, not to the top level.
.I "*"
matches every subject,
.I <name>
is an exact subject match,
.I *group:<g>*
matches a JWT
.I groups
claim containing
.IR <g> .
When
.B auth.mode
is not
.IR none ,
a topic without an ACL rejects every connection.
.SH EXAMPLES
See
.IR /usr/share/zerodds/configs/ws-bridged.yaml.example .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-ws-bridged (1),
.BR zerodds-xmlc (1).
